<h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
<p class="lede">
  A plain page with no bindings. It exists to show that a route can render a
  page that needs nothing from the request.
</p>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>What this starter is</h2>
  <p>
    Pages are NXL templates. Statements run where you put them, and values are
    escaped when they are printed. The whole page compiles and runs on the
    server for each request.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is not a framework. There is no client-side bundler, no component model
    and no virtual DOM — the browser receives finished HTML.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>Where things live</h2>
  <dl class="defs">
    <dt><code>pages/</code></dt>
    <dd>One file per route, named by the <code>page</code> key in <code>nxl.toml</code>.</dd>
    <dt><code>layouts/</code></dt>
    <dd>Wrapped around every page. <code>&lt;nxl raw="content" /&gt;</code> is where the page goes.</dd>
    <dt><code>public/</code></dt>
    <dd>Static assets, served as-is.</dd>
    <dt><code>src/</code></dt>
    <dd>The NXL program that <code>nexora dev</code> compiles for the browser.</dd>
  </dl>
</section>